  "force_reason": "BRTI end to end: venue bar series, venue strike and venue settlement, so bars, barrier and label are all the series the markets settle on. Coinbase bars misplaced the venue settlement on 184 of 6,009 windows (3.1%) against 1 for BRTI. Taker, not maker: resting saved 0.94pp/contract of fee and cost 1.85pp to adverse selection, and there is no exit path, so a resting order pays a market maker cost and earns none of the revenue. cross_venue and implied_vol are both out under --complete-cases: implied_vol holds 2,047 SOL fits against 50,924 for BTC and discarded nearly every SOL row, and pm_market_probability was the single largest dropper at 46,514 of 79,308 rows; without them coverage is 98.8% and folds even out to 1,953-1,992 windows. cross_venue was the only group producing tradeable disagreement (trade rate 1.48% against 0.04%) but that disagreement lost money (-0.53pp realised over 528 trades), and with a peer sampled every ~16s it is largely lagged momentum. The shipped shrinkage is the WALK-FORWARD median, not the refit own inner-holdout fit: the refit estimates it on ~10% of training windows and returned 0.00001 against a walk-forward 0.96-1.00, which makes the model emit the market price and refuse every trade. Standing operator policy: the Sunday retrain ALWAYS installs so the model keeps absorbing new data; the gates are advisory and the operator reads them.",
